course: dictionary
lesson: 8858
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning a number, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it first. «She is a great shooter, and she scored three goals.» Here shooter means a player who shoots at goal, not a gun.
explain: Shooter can mean a person who fires a gun, arrow or ball, a gun in informal talk, or a video game where you shoot things. Ask yourself which meaning fits the clues. A game about aliens points to a video game. A netball match points to a player.
explain: Be careful with news reports. «Many were killed by snipers (hidden shooters).» Here a shooter is someone who fired a gun and hurt people. It is a serious, frightening meaning, so it is never a word to joke with.
fact: A shooter can be a person who shoots a gun, an arrow or a ball.
fact: In netball and basketball, the shooter is the player who shoots at goal and scores.
fact: In games, a shooter is a video game where players shoot things, such as a «first-person shooter».
fact: A «straight shooter» is an honest person.
fact: In the news, «shooter» means someone who fired a gun and hurt people, and it is a serious word.
exercise: «She is the goal shooter, and she scored ten goals today.» In netball, what is a goal shooter? | A bird that sings at night | A person who cooks the dinner | *A player who shoots at goal and scores | A gun
exercise: «My brother plays a first-person shooter.» What does shooter mean here? | *A video game where players shoot things | A netball player | A basketball coach | A person who fired a gun
exercise: «Dad is a straight shooter, so he always tells the truth.» What does straight shooter mean? | A person who shoots straight at a target | A person who sings loudly | A person who is always late | *An honest person
test: What does shooter mean in «Sam hid the shooter under his coat»? | A goal shooter in netball | A video game | A bird that sings | *A gun
test: Why does the word shooter have more than one meaning? | Because the dictionary is wrong | *Because one word can have several meanings, and the context shows which one | Because it is always a misspelling | Because it is always about a gun
exam: In «The shooter scored in the last second», which meaning fits best? | A person who paints pictures | A video game about aliens | *A player who shoots at goal and scores | A gun that fires at a wall
